35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The data is clear. Compliance projects finish on time, but comfort-driven ones slip a year.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,The timetable shows we paid for off-site space for two terms. Specialist rooms sit idle.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The freeze left posts empty, yet technicians still perform manual checks weekly. We waste labor.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,Surveys in older blocks keep finding hazardous material. The last two openings added months.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The reserve is empty. We bought expensive gear, wrote it off, and forgot to fund replacement.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, compliance is necessary, but not sufficient. My data shows shared access drives satisfaction.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, shared access is vital, but my data shows the real cost is displaced students.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, you’re right. We can’t ignore the staffing gap. We must pick a plan that doesn’t stretch us.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, valid concern. But if we choose compliance, the schedule holds. We must prioritize safety.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, compliance is cheap. The real hemorrhage is the empty reserve. We are borrowing from the future.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the empty reserve is a symptom. My data proves shared access drives satisfaction.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, the empty reserve is a symptom of poor planning. My data proves we pay for empty rooms.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, the empty reserve is a symptom of ignoring maintenance. We cannot fund new projects by starving staff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, the reserve is critical, but my data shows compliance projects finish on time.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, symptoms are cheap to fix. The structural rot is the empty reserve. We are borrowing from our own future.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@All, we must choose a plan that respects the schedule and doesn’t break the budget.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@All, we must stop paying for off-site space. We need a plan that solves the actual shortage.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@All, we need a plan that reduces our team’s daily manual labor. That relief is non-negotiable.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@All, we must prioritize projects that benefit the whole campus, not just one wing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@All, we must avoid plans that require us to borrow from our own future.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
